  "body": "feat(wire): closing overlap, centre-line slit and open-run skims for Wire Contour\r\n\r\nWire Contour gains the three polish cuts of #3216. Each is stated, never\r\ninferred, and refused by name where it has nothing to state.\r\n\r\nWhat changed\r\n\r\n- Closing overlap (closed profiles). `WireContourOp.overlap` and\r\n  `WireParams.overlap` (mm, default 0) ride the cut past the seam by the\r\n  stated arc length before the lead-out returns to the threading point,\r\n  so the start of the cut is burnt over and no witness mark is left.\r\n  The past-seam extension walks the ring from the seam point and cuts\r\n  the last point to the exact remainder; the kerf law judges the return\r\n  move like every other. Refused: with tabs (tabs pin the seam), on an\r\n  open run (no seam), at a negative or non-finite length. A skim\r\n  inherits the overlap. The note says the ride.\r\n- Centre-line slit (open runs). New `WireSide::Centre`: the wire rides\r\n  the run itself, the kerf burns both sides, no side is kept - so the\r\n  kerf law has no product to protect and is not applied, while the\r\n  corner/doubling-back law and the run-out laws still refuse what the\r\n  wire cannot follow. The note says \"no side kept\".\r\n- Skims on open runs. `check_passes` no longer refuses an open run; the\r\n  offset-ordering laws judge it like a closed profile. `wire_passes`\r\n  routes each open-side skim through the open-run generator: every pass\r\n  re-enters from the air at the run's start end, at its own run-in\r\n  point, walked in the run's own direction - a reversed pass on an open\r\n  run is refused by name (one pinned semantic), and no move joins one\r\n  pass's run-out to the next pass's run-in (the wire is threaded anew).\r\n- Wire verify (sim). `CutSide::Centre` is judged as an open run whose\r\n  kerf law is skipped by statement (`CENTRE_SKIP` on the report line);\r\n  the ends' clearance is still judged. Skims on an open run are\r\n  generated but named as not verified here yet (the verify reads one\r\n  open pass) - a follow-up can extend the open law to per-pass kerfs.\r\n- App, file and UI. The overlap rides the seed, the command door's\r\n  sanity, the op stamp (only when stated, so no existing stamp moves)\r\n  and the project DTO (`overlap`, absent reads 0); `side` reads and\r\n  writes `centre`. The wire page gains the Closing overlap row and the\r\n  Centre choice; its test count grows by one.\r\n\r\nPinning tests\r\n\r\n- `the_closing_overlap_rides_past_the_seam_and_is_refused_without_a_seam`\r\n  (camcraft_motion::wire_edm): ride length past the seam, inherited\r\n  skim ride, lead-out home, and each refusal by name.\r\n- `a_centre_slit_rides_the_run_itself_and_takes_skims_from_the_air`\r\n  (camcraft_motion::wire_edm): centre ride on the line, air threading\r\n  per pass at its own offset, reversed refused.\r\n- `skim_laws_refuse_by_name`: the open-run skim refusal is replaced by\r\n  the offset laws accepting it.\r\n- `wire_closing_overlap_and_centre_side_apply_and_undo` (camcraft-ui).\r\n\r\nReadings: the overlap ride of 1.0 mm on a 40x20 die ends at\r\n(1.000, -9.835) with K = 0.165; a centre slit's left skim threads at\r\n(60.000, -1.145) against the rough's (60.000, -1.165).\r\n\r\nNot exercised\r\n\r\n- The Sodick post refuses an open run's skims by name at its rapid\r\n  guard: its manual states no such pass structure, and the generic ISO\r\n  post is the one that cuts, travels and threads anew around each\r\n  boundary.\r\n\r\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`, 665 steps)\r\n\r\n- All sim, motion, app and ui suites green, the three pinning tests\r\n  included.\r\n- Three steps are red, each not caused by this change:\r\n  - `app suites: docs_troubleshooting` - the stem of a clearance\r\n    message spans a line-continued string in `crates/sim/src/verify`;\r\n    no file of this change is in its sources.\r\n  - `app suites: example_catalog` (2d/drill-overfeed) - the fixture\r\n    `refusal.txt` on disk reads CRLF against the generated LF; a\r\n    checkout line-ending state, no fixture touched here.\r\n  - `ui suites: lib` - a native STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION at 20 test\r\n    threads after all tests printed ok; it re-runs green in full\r\n    (`1431 passed; 0 failed`) and at 1 and 4 threads. A teardown race\r\n    of the headless window harness on this machine, not this change.\r\n\r\nScreenshots (images only on the fork's pr-screenshots branch)\r\n\r\n- Controls, before: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr3617-wire-controls-before.png\r\n- Controls, after (the new Closing overlap row and its help): https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr3617-wire-controls-after.png\r\n- Full window, before: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr3617-wire-window-before.png\r\n- Full window, after: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr3617-wire-window-after.png\r\n\r\nRework after the safety review (head 795d69e95)\r\n\r\nThe eight review items of 2026-11-25 are addressed on the same branch:\r\n\r\n1. The Centre slit's run-out clearance joins the generation stamp\r\n   (cutting.rs), so an edited or re-stated clearance reads Stale -\r\n   pinned through the edit command and a project reload (wire_stamp).\r\n2. The overlap's ride includes the seam edge's own remainder back to\r\n   the seam: a 100 mm overlap covers exactly 100 mm of arc, forward\r\n   and reversed, and a ride longer than one full lap is refused by\r\n   name (motion tests, both directions, near the perimeter).\r\n3. An open run's skim passes are rethreaded in the air: a travel move\r\n   (a rapid, no wire through it) marks each pass boundary, the wire\r\n   verify judges each pass at its own kerf and its own ends, and the\r\n   generic ISO post cuts, travels and threads anew around it - a new\r\n   app test generates, verifies AND posts an open run with a skim\r\n   (new goldens wire_contour_open_skims.nc and wire_contour_centre_skims.nc).\r\n4. A stated overlap beside a no-core burnout is refused by name at the\r\n   command door (create and edit tested).\r\n5. A stated overlap on a 4-axis cut and beside a constant taper is\r\n   refused by name at the command door (the 3-degree/1 mm case that\r\n   once failed with \"repeats a point\" now refuses at the door;\r\n   create and edit tested per combination).\r\n6. The three-file merge with current main keeps both sides; the\r\n   resolved tree builds and its gates run (below).\r\n7. Before / after screenshots of the changed Wire Contour controls\r\n   are on the fork's pr-screenshots branch and linked below.\r\n8. This PR edits .claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md; the body\r\n   carries the process line. PROCESS_VERSION is untouched.\r\n\r\nThe choice per item is recorded in\r\ndocs/decisions/3216-wire-overlap-rework.md: items 2 and 3 are defects\r\nof what the feature claims, so they are implemented properly; items 4\r\nand 5 are refused by name at the command door, safer than a\r\nhalf-implemented overlap on the burnout, 4-axis and taper builders.\r\n\r\nMain moved while the rework ran (the wire exit pick, the arc joins, the rotary stated axis, the tool preview), so the branch carries one more merge of current main, resolved keeping both sides, and the gates below ran on the refreshed head.\r\n\r\nGates on the resolved tree: motion lib 668 passed, sim lib 253 passed, app lib 311 passed, ui lib 1659 passed; mcp_wire_contour 8, wire_verify 3, golden_cl 34, wire_post 13, wire_stamp 8, wire_contour 19, wire_burnout 4, wire_taper 11, wire_4axis 8, wire_verify_tol 4,\r\nconformance 7 (every builtin posts every golden byte exact), the\r\nsodick wire suites, g_edm_post, agie_native; clippy app + motion + sim\r\n+ ui --all-targets -D warnings clean. example_catalog's\r\n2d/drill-overfeed refusal.txt CRLF red is the known environmental\r\n#3628, unrelated to this diff (41 of its steps pass).\r\n\r\nChangelog: Wire Contour: a stated closing overlap rides the cut past its seam; a centre-line slit side for open runs; skim passes on open runs re-entered from the air.\r\n\r\nfork synced at v0.25.0\r\n\r\nProcess change: yes\r\n\r\nFixes #3216\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
